{"transcript":"ˌdɪsɪnˈtʃæntmənt","exists":true,"definitions":["A feeling of disappointment about someone or something previously admired.","A state of no longer believing in something good or positive."],"examples":["The disenchantment with politics grew.","Her disenchantment was evident.","A period of disenchantment followed."],"lemma":"disenchant","lemmaPos":"verb","synonyms":["disillusionment","disappointment","disillusion"],"number":"singular","pluralForm":"disenchantments","source":"disenchantment"}